:"L-wing, beside the Performing Arts Center","notes":"Meet in L-wing and take in the current exhibition at your own pace. Check the gallery page before going, since exhibitions and public hours change seasonally.","short_summary":"Free public access to changing exhibitions on the Galloway campus.","evidence_claim":"Stockton University Art Gallery states that it is free and open to the public during exhibitions and is located in L-wing beside the Performing Arts Center.","source_url":"https://stockton.edu/art-gallery/","source_title":"Art Gallery","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free and open to the public during exhibitions. The gallery lists seasonal hours and notes that weekday visitor parking requirements may apply before 3 p.m.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"stockton-overlook-lounge-charging","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Overlook Lounge Charging Station","title":"Recharge and catch up in Overlook Lounge","subtitle":"Campus Center, upper level","notes":"Bring devices and use the charging station while your group works or talks in the lounge. The space also has seating, tables, TV viewing, and monitor-equipped worktables.","short_summary":"A free device-charging stop with lounge seating and collaborative work space.","evidence_claim":"Stockton says its Campus Center charging stations are available free of charge and identifies one in Overlook Lounge, which also has lounge furniture and worktables.","source_url":"https://stockton.edu/campus-center/operations/index.html","source_title":"Campus Center Operations","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located on the Campus Center’s second level. The charging station is free of charge; use the lounge respectfully around other students’ study and group-work needs.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"stockton-coffeehouse-charging-station","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Coffee House Charging Station","title":"Plug in at the Coffee House","subtitle":"Campus Center, main level","notes":"Use the free Coffee House charging station as a meet-up point, then settle into the shared hangout area to talk, read, or plan the rest of your day.","short_summary":"A no-purchase charging stop in Stockton’s central Coffee House.","evidence_claim":"Stockton says Campus Center charging stations are available free of charge and lists one in the Coffeehouse on the main level.","source_url":"https://stockton.edu/campus-center/operations/index.html","source_title":"Campus Center Operations","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Main-level Campus Center Coffee House. The charging station is free of charge; buying food or drinks is not required to use that amenity.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"stockton-bjork-library-public-access","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Richard E. Bjork Library","title":"Read or study in Bjork Library","subtitle":"E-wing Library, Galloway campus","notes":"Choose an open table, carrel, chair, or lounge seat and make it a quiet shared work session. Keep group conversation to the Learning Commons and respect designated quiet areas.","short_summary":"Open library spaces for reading, viewing materials, and study.","evidence_claim":"Stockton’s library-space procedure designates open library spaces as public access areas and makes them available to library users for study, reading, and use of materials.","source_url":"https://stockton.edu/policy-procedure/documents/procedures/4109.pdf","source_title":"Use of Library Space Procedure","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open spaces, including tables, chairs, carrels, and lounge furniture, are public access areas on a first-come basis. Group study rooms are restricted to Stockton students and employees with reservations.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"stockton-information-desk-push-cart","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Campus Center Information & Operations Desk Push Carts","title":"Borrow a push cart for a group haul","subtitle":"Campus Center Grand Hall, main level","notes":"If your group is moving supplies or projects across campus, ask at the Information & Operations Desk for a push cart and return it after the trip.","short_summary":"Free push-cart borrowing from the Campus Center desk.","evidence_claim":"Stockton states that push carts are available from the Campus Center Information & Operations Desk and that cart rentals are free of charge.","source_url":"https://stockton.edu/campus-center/operations/index.html","source_title":"Campus Center Operations","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Request a push cart from the Information & Operations Desk during its regular business hours. Coordinate with desk staff on checkout and return.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
